OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 29 Nov to Tue 8 DecFFor
OL,6,Fthe end of November and into early
OL,7,FDecember, Atlantic frontal systems are
OL,8,Flikely to try and make inroads from
OL,9,Fthe west, though the eastwards
OL,10,Fprogression of bands of rain is
OL,11,Funcertain. As such, western or
OL,12,Fnorthwestern areas are likely to be
OL,13,Fwettest, with potential for strong
OL,14,Fwinds at times too. Southeastern areas
OL,15,Fare most likely to remain drier
OL,16,Foverall. Temperatures may become a
OL,17,Flittle milder than recent days, though
OL,18,Fthere remains the potential for
OL,19,Fovernight frost and fog where skies
OL,20,Fare clear and winds fall light.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
